   "description": "<p><strong>What you will do</strong></p>\n<p>Currently, we are looking for someone who can fill the position of Part Time Mandarin Teacher. Take a look at some points below to understand more about this role.</p>\n<p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Plan, organize, and implement oral and written Mandarin language teaching programs.</li>\n  <li>Manage Mandarin classes for diverse target audiences (children, teenagers, and adults) across various levels and needs (beginners, daily conversation, Business Mandarin, and HSK/HSKK test preparation).</li>\n  <li>Periodically evaluate students' learning progress and provide clear, constructive reports.</li>\n  <li>Collaborate in designing engaging visual learning materials (as needed).</li>\n  <li>Accurately assess students' proficiency levels in accordance with current HSK levelling standards.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Core Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Bachelor’s degree (S1) in Chinese Literature, Mandarin Education, or graduated from a university in China. Other majors are welcome to apply provided they have equivalent Mandarin proficiency and skills.</li>\n  <li>Mandatory Mandarin proficiency certification (HSK 2.0): Minimum HSK Level 4 (HSK 5 &amp; 6 are highly preferred) and HSKK (minimum Intermediate level (中级), Advanced level (高级) preferred).</li></ul>",
